<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Commission of Government</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1934">1934</a>–<a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Commission of Government was the unelected body that governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> from 1934 to 1949. Facing bankruptcy in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>, the dominion gave up self-government, and a governor and six commissioners appointed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, three from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and three from Newfoundland, took over. It ended when Newfoundland joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> as its tenth province in 1949.</p></div>
